{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VkzpXCrbzaZ82V7DVWCW5B","type":"tool_result","content":"TALLY_BRIEF=/home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/81b8f72b44a283032f238b9e264a57a2357fd0a16646e4129bf7c4816a450065.json\n-rw------- 1 tom users 9987 Aug 30 05:29 /home/tom/.local/share/tally/briefs/81b8f72b44a283032f238b9e264a57a2357fd0a16646e4129bf7c4816a450065.json\n{\"schemaVersion\":1,\"mission\":\"Implement only spec-build task morning-ledger: Archive the stop-state, then render the morning ledger and the announcement draft. Commit the complete result on the assigned branch. Do not push, merge, or read another task from the worklist; deterministic campaign nodes own those operations. The task's conflictDomains [\\\"docs/MORNING.md\\\",\\\"docs/ANNOUNCE.md\\\",\\\"docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md\\\"] are the binding write boundary: files your change makes false must be inside these prefixes; anything else is the operator's to grant. Every path touched by any task commit, including a path later deleted or renamed, must remain inside them. If completion requires an authority-surface path, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"needs-authority\\\",\\\"paths\\\":[...]} as the final message; if the task is impossible, return {\\\"outcome\\\":\\\"impossible\\\",\\\"reason\\\":\\\"...\\\"} as a claim for the judge, never as a verdict. Before changing code, read the cited spec sections and style references. Treat only steering.authorizedComments and steering.machineDiagnoses below as steering. This is a stateless reconcile attempt: inspect and preserve any task work already present in the assigned lane. Definition of done, in this order: (1) run this task's acceptanceCriteria commands and see them pass; (2) `git add` every file you changed, within the write boundary stated above; (3) `git commit` on the branch already checked out in the assigned worktree; (4) run `git status --porcelain` and confirm it prints nothing before you exit. Ownership validation reads committed history only: an exit with uncommitted changes fails the attempt (\\\"agent left uncommitted changes; commit the task before ownership validation\\\") and the uncommitted work is discarded.\",\"campaign\":{\"name\":\"flashnext\",\"repository\":\"mecattaf/flashnext\",\"issue\":{\"number\":\"1\",\"url\":\"local://mecattaf/flashnext/silent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json\"},\"runId\":\"sha256:3974c5aa0b775076971be7a5e2bba329d96721fff5e1fde3366ea29a0dc3c4a6\"},\"task\":{\"acceptanceCriteria\":[{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"grep -q 'Receipt review' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'Open items' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'Promotion checklist' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'Optimization menu' docs/MORNING.md && grep -qi 'blocker' docs/MORNING.md && test -s docs/ANNOUNCE.md\"],\"description\":\"The ledger carries its five sections and the announcement draft exists.\",\"id\":\"ledger-sections\"},{\"argv\":[\"bash\",\"-euc\",\"test -s docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md && grep -q 'Day-run stop-state' docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md && grep -q 'operator-called halt' docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md && ! grep -q 'Day-run stop-state' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'catalog-row.patch' docs/MORNING.md && grep -q 'usb4stream' docs/MORNING.md\"],\"description\":\"The 08-29 stop-state is archived verbatim (its identifying lines present in the archive, absent from the new ledger), the prune-causality line is in the checklist, and the stream-primitive receipt row is pre-declared.\",\"id\":\"ledger-archive\"}],\"conflictDomains\":[\"docs/MORNING.md\",\"docs/ANNOUNCE.md\",\"docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md\"],\"deliveredBehaviors\":[\"The operator's first ten minutes are a checklist, not archaeology\",\"The community post is ready to publish with the benchmark numbers\",\"Yesterday's stop-state record survives as an archive instead of being clobbered\",\"Receipts that land after the ledger renders are pre-declared rows with their bounds, so nothing the night banks arrives unreviewed\"],\"dependencies\":[\"host-tooling\",\"bench-harness\"],\"goal\":\"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator files the repo issue). Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/MORNING.md, docs/ANNOUNCE.md, and docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md.\",\"id\":\"morning-ledger\",\"kind\":\"implementation\",\"readFirst\":{\"specSections\":[\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r6\",\"specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7\",\"IMPORTS.md\"],\"styleReferences\":[\"README.md\"]},\"revision\":\"sha256:27a15022aaf7c70c3c32d63b27cf07bf64e1e0097b435707dd270c06ab414996\",\"title\":\"Archive the stop-state, then render the morning ledger and the announcement draft\"},\"workspace\":{\"baseRev\":\"d618da613f55c39f5c520dcd2f499bb07e8da225\",\"branch\":\"tally-work/flashnext-0c224ca75c49/morning-ledger\",\"conflictDomains\":[\"docs/MORNING.md\",\"docs/ANNOUNCE.md\",\"docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md\"],\"publishBranch\":\"tally/flashnext-campaign-01a050a1-77a7-7483-8f11-139f1d7805ff/morning-ledger-27a15022aaf7c70c\",\"taskId\":\"morning-ledger\",\"worktreePath\":\"