{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XYyJsZgdanPdpZ7CVRobYN","type":"tool_result","content":"scripts/run-smoke.sh:4:# answered before any weight byte moves. Writes results/receipts/smoke.json.\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:8:OUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/smoke.json\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:54:# Receipt quarantine (D12): a fail receipt lands under results/receipts/\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:58:base = \"/results/receipts\" if r[\"status\"] == \"pass\" else \"/results/receipts/failed\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:63:echo \"smoke receipt: $OUT (fail receipts land under results/receipts/failed/)\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:67:ok = root / \"results/receipts/smoke.json\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:68:failed = root / \"results/receipts/failed/smoke.json\"\nscripts/build-engine.sh:30:RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\nscripts/receipts-verify.py:2:\"\"\"Validate every overnight receipt under results/receipts/.\nscripts/receipts-verify.py:119:    # Quarantined failure receipts (results/receipts/failed/) are typed\ntests/test_host_tooling.py:193:        self.assertIn(\"results/receipts\", self.runner)\ntests/test_host_tooling.py:196:                      \"under results/receipts/failed/\")\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:13:# Writes results/receipts/preflight.json and exits non-zero on any hard\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:23:RECEIPT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/preflight.json\"\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:179:# results/receipts/failed/ — committed, ledger-reviewed, a typed blocker —\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:183:  RECEIPT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/failed/preflight.json\"\nscripts/stage-weights-both.sh:7:# and installed to results/receipts/weights-<host>.json only when its status\nscripts/stage-weights-both.sh:8:# is pass; a fail receipt lands under results/receipts/failed/ instead — a\nscripts/stage-weights-both.sh:14:RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\nscripts/run-tp2.sh:16:# results/receipts/failed/<step>.json — committed and ledger-reviewed as a\nscripts/run-tp2.sh:26:RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\ncontainer/build.sh:34:OUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/build.json\"\ncontainer/build.sh:36:# container/ and results/receipts/ write boundary is ever created or left\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:95:      \"goal\": \"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\"build\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:124:        \"results/receipts\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:240:      \"goal\": \"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:261:            \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:299:        \"results/receipts/proxy.json\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:306:      \"goal\": \"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator files the repo issue). Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/MORNING.md, docs/ANNOUNCE.md, and docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:449:        \"bash container/build.sh && python3 -c \\\"import json,subprocess,sys; head=json.loads(subprocess.run(['git','show','HEAD:results/receipts/build.json'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout); new=json.load(open('results/receipts/build.json')); inv=('torch','triton','fork_commit'); ok=(new.get('status')=='pass'==head.get('status') and all(new['data'].get(k)==head['data'].get(k) for k in inv)); subprocess.run(['git','checkout','--','results/receipts/build.json'],check=True) if ok else sys.exit('cp-build: receipt drift on contract fields: '+repr({k:(head['data'].get(k),new['data'].get(k)) for k in inv if head['data'].get(k)!=new['data'].get(k)}))\\\"\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:534:      \"goal\": \"Author (never run — the dead-last checkpoint runs it) a wedge-safe first-light benchmark of the in-tree USB4 stream primitive, as transport-decision evidence for the morning. Deliverables: (1) bench/usb4stream-bench.py — one file serving both roles (coordinator role is the default; peer role via --role peer --dev PATH; the peer is launched by streaming this same file over the control wire: ssh worker with the script on stdin, never a copy). Non-negotiable mechanics, each existing because an open/close storm against a mismatched peer wedges router hop tables and already darkened rail 0 once: (a) NEVER hardcode a numbered device node and never write a digit directly after the word tbstream anywhere in the file — the numbering is asymmetric across the twins and the coordinator carries PEERLESS cable-B groups at the low indices, where a blocking open waits forever; resolve on EACH node as: the rail netdev carrying the 10.99.0.0/30 address, then readlink /sys/class/net/RAIL/device, then the parent xdomain, then the sibling service whose key attribute is stream, then the configfs group fn0's index attribute, then the device node /dev/tbstream suffixed with that index; require BOTH ends' fn0 configfs groups to exist before any open. (b) Exactly ONE open attempt per side, ever, blocking, under a 30 s alarm; any failure after that point: close whatever is open, kill the ssh child, write the receipt, exit — never reopen, never retry, never write configfs (read ring_size and throttling only). (c) Idempotence guard: if results/receipts/usb4stream.json already exists, exit 0 immediately WITHOUT touching any device — this is what makes harness retries storm-free by construction. (d) Skip preconditions, checked in this order BEFORE any device access, each producing receipt status pass with data.outcome 'skipped:REASON' and exit 0: (i) the pair serve is up — the API answers on the coordinator, or podman reports the serving container running on either node (check the worker over the control wire) — outcome 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable': the stream device shares cable A with the serving rails and a wedge would take the campaign's headline deliverable down, so this bench runs ONLY on an idle cable; (ii) ping -c1 -W2 to the rail peer fails — outcome 'skipped:rail-peer-unreachable'; (iii) either end's fn0 configfs group is missing — outcome 'skipped:configfs-group-missing'. Record data.serve_up true or false in EVERY receipt including skips. (e) Fixed schedule, no adaptivity, no retries: 50 iterations of 4 KiB ping-pong warmup (discarded); RTT at 64, 4096, 16384, 65536 bytes times 500 iterations with p50 and p99 per size; the allreduce-shaped simultaneous exchange at 8192, 16384, 65536 bytes times 500 (both sides write N bytes then read N bytes — ring 1024 times 4 KiB frames buffers this safely); throughput 256 MiB each direction; under 90 s wall total, whole run under a global timeout. (f) The receipt at results/receipts/usb4stream.json: one JSON object, step 'usb4stream', status ALWAYS 'pass' — this bench is evidence-gathering, not a campaign claim, so a mid-run abort is typed as data.outcome 'aborted:PHASE:ERRNO' rather than a fail status that would redden every later gate run; data carries outcome, per-size rtt and exchange p50/p99 fields, throughput both directions, ring_size and throttling as read from configfs, resolved device paths on both ends, open_count (assert exactly 1 per side), serve_up, and loop 'python' for honesty about syscall-loop overhead. (2) scripts/receipts-verify.py: add a 'usb4stream' entry to the BOUNDS table — outcome 'ok' requires open_count 1 and all schedule fields present; 'skipped:' and 'aborted:' outcomes require their reason text and pass. (3) docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md — the decision memo: why the collective-library net-plugin route is REJECTED for the latency goal (it sits under the library's proxy and protocol stack, HopID scarcity shared with the network paths forces a multiplexer over one or two long-lived streams, and comm teardown on every serve restart is exactly the open/close pattern the wedge hazard forbids; 3-5 attended days to a fragile prototype, 2-4 attended weeks to overnight-trustworthy); why the real path is a 2-4 attended-day port of the reference doorbell-plus-progress-thread allreduce (the 105 microsecond reference bar) from verbs onto the stream device's read and write, with the receive path run by the progress thread; the morning trigger criteria (banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix showing allreduce-dominated decode); the note that after a healthy night the first real run happens attended in the morning AFTER the pair is torn down (the serve-up skip is deliberate); and a drafted-not-filed issue body for the port. (4) tests/test_usb4stream_bench.py: py-compile both edited python files, assert the no-hardcoded-device-node invariant (no digit after tbstream in the bench source), assert the idempotence guard and the serve-up skip are present, and exercise the receipts checker's three outcome branches with synthetic receipt dicts. Boundaries: touch only bench/usb4stream-bench.py, docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md, scripts/receipts-verify.py, and tests/.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:588:      \"goal\": \"Measure whether the ROCm 10.0.0 substrate is viable for this fork on this hardware, without touching the 7.14 lane that served the night. Context: a complete aligned gfx1151/cp312 wheel set exists at https://stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-next/ (verified 2026-08-30; wheels dated 2026-08-26; same upstream versions and the SAME triton git hash 4cff872c as the current pins, so the swap is a pure version-literal substitution) — but no upstream anywhere has run this engine on ROCm 10 on gfx1151, and two failure modes are unmeasured: whether ROCm 10's hipcc compiles the fork's HIP sources, and whether its HSA runtime binds to the in-tree KFD on this kernel. This lane answers both as DATA. Build a second image flashnext:rocm10 from the UNMODIFIED container/Containerfile using its existing build ARGs (ROCM_WHL, TORCH_PIN, TORCHVISION_PIN, TRITON_PIN, ROCM_DEVEL_PIN, DEVICE_PINS at container/Containerfile:48-65 — no recipe edit, so the banked container-recipe acceptance stays true): podman build --tag flashnext:rocm10 --file container/Containerfile --build-arg ROCM_WHL=https://stable.repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-next/ --build-arg 'TORCH_PIN=torch==2.13.0+rocm10.0.0' --build-arg 'TORCHVISION_PIN=torchvision==0.28.0+rocm10.0.0' --build-arg 'TRITON_PIN=triton==3.8.0+git4cff872c.rocm10.0.0' --build-arg 'ROCM_DEVEL_PIN=rocm-sdk-devel==10.0.0' --build-arg 'DEVICE_PINS=amd-torch-device-gfx1151==2.13.0+rocm10.0.0 amd-torchvision-device-gfx1151==0.28.0+rocm10.0.0 rocm-sdk-device-gfx1151==10.0.0' . (a prefetched wheel set may exist under ~/.cache/flashnext-wheels/rocm10/). Then, on the coordinator only, run a minimal GPU binding check in that image (--device /dev/kfd --device /dev/dri --security-opt seccomp=unconfined --ipc=host): torch.cuda.is_available(), torch.cuda.get_device_properties(0).gcnArchName, a small fp16 and a small fp8-block matmul, and importing the engine package. Record the ROCm/HSA and KFD versions the runtime reports plus the running kernel release (a green probe on a 7.2.0 coordinator is strong but not conclusive for the pair; a red probe attributable to KFD must be re-checked on 7.2.2 before ROCm 10 is written off — say so in the notes field). Do not load the checkpoint, do not start a server, do not touch the worker. WRITE THE RECEIPT TO results/rocm10-probe.json — NOT under results/receipts/: scripts/receipts-verify.py fails the campaign gate on any fail-status receipt in that directory, and this lane exists to record an outcome, green or red, never to fail the campaign. The receipt carries {step:'rocm10-probe', status, ts, data:{build_ok, compile_seconds, torch, triton, rocm_sdk_core, gcn_arch, cuda_available, matmul_fp16_ok, matmul_fp8_block_ok, engine_import_ok, kernel_release, notes}} with status 'pass' whenever an outcome was recorded. Never remove or retag flashnext:dev; never edit container/, results/receipts/, or the worklist. If the night is running late this lane is the first thing the operator drops. Boundaries: touch only results/rocm10-probe.json.\",","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c18f0a4-02d1-4d56-a81b-3d63fcd0659e","uuid":"ec8087af-c9be-4b85-bde4-4253a57d0d88","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:29:52.052Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"scripts/run-smoke.sh:4:# answered before any weight byte moves. Writes results/receipts/smoke.json.\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:8:OUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/smoke.json\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:54:# Receipt quarantine (D12): a fail receipt lands under results/receipts/\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:58:base = \"/results/receipts\" if r[\"status\"] == \"pass\" else \"/results/receipts/failed\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:63:echo \"smoke receipt: $OUT (fail receipts land under results/receipts/failed/)\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:67:ok = root / \"results/receipts/smoke.json\"\nscripts/run-smoke.sh:68:failed = root / \"results/receipts/failed/smoke.json\"\nscripts/build-engine.sh:30:RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\nscripts/receipts-verify.py:2:\"\"\"Validate every overnight receipt under results/receipts/.\nscripts/receipts-verify.py:119:    # Quarantined failure receipts (results/receipts/failed/) are typed\ntests/test_host_tooling.py:193:        self.assertIn(\"results/receipts\", self.runner)\ntests/test_host_tooling.py:196:                      \"under results/receipts/failed/\")\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:13:# Writes results/receipts/preflight.json and exits non-zero on any hard\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:23:RECEIPT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/preflight.json\"\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:179:# results/receipts/failed/ — committed, ledger-reviewed, a typed blocker —\nhost/fn-preflight.sh:183:  RECEIPT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/failed/preflight.json\"\nscripts/stage-weights-both.sh:7:# and installed to results/receipts/weights-<host>.json only when its status\nscripts/stage-weights-both.sh:8:# is pass; a fail receipt lands under results/receipts/failed/ instead — a\nscripts/stage-weights-both.sh:14:RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\nscripts/run-tp2.sh:16:# results/receipts/failed/<step>.json — committed and ledger-reviewed as a\nscripts/run-tp2.sh:26:RECEIPTS=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts\"\ncontainer/build.sh:34:OUT=\"$REPO_ROOT/results/receipts/build.json\"\ncontainer/build.sh:36:# container/ and results/receipts/ write boundary is ever created or left\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:95:      \"goal\": \"THE PRIMARY ENGINE LANE of spec ruling P4 (the nix wiring in the tree is the graduation lane — leave it alone). Write container/Containerfile and container/build.sh implementing IMPORTS.md sections 1 and 2 and spec claim 3.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r3), designed for overnight iteration: the fork checkout and its build directory are bind-mounted volumes with ccache enabled so a one-line patch rebuild recompiles only what changed, and the image can be entered for edit-and-restart iteration without a rebuild. Containerfile: Ubuntu 24.04; python 3.12 venv at /opt/venv; install torch 2.13.0+rocm7.14.0 and torchvision 0.28.0+rocm7.14.0 and the matching triton wheel from the vendor stable index https://repo.amd.com/rocm/whl-multi-arch/ (record the exact resolved triton version); git clone --depth 1 --branch flashnext https://github.com/mecattaf/vllm and build it from source against those wheels for GPU target gfx1151 (relax nothing: the torch pin is satisfied exactly; drop audio extras rather than adding torchaudio); COPY container/rootfs/ into site-packages so the fn_ instrument modules land importable; write /opt/flashnext/build-info.json inside the image carrying the fork commit, torch, triton, and image build time. build.sh: run the packaging tests first, then podman build tagged flashnext:dev, then write results/receipts/build.json as {step:\\\"build\\\", status, ts, data:{torch, triton, fork_commit, image_digest}} with status fail on any error. Credit the recipe shape to the MIT toolbox recipe named in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md in the Containerfile header. Boundaries: touch only container/ and results/receipts/.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:124:        \"results/receipts\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:240:      \"goal\": \"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:261:            \"bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:299:        \"results/receipts/proxy.json\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:306:      \"goal\": \"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator files the repo issue). Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/MORNING.md, docs/ANNOUNCE.md, and docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:449:        \"bash container/build.sh && python3 -c \\\"import json,subprocess,sys; head=json.loads(subprocess.run(['git','show','HEAD:results/receipts/build.json'],capture_output=True,text=True,check=True).stdout); new=json.load(open('results/receipts/build.json')); inv=('torch','triton','fork_commit'); ok=(new.get('status')=='pass'==head.get('status') and all(new['data'].get(k)==head['data'].get(k) for k in inv)); subprocess.run(['git','checkout','--','results/receipts/build.json'],check=True) if ok else sys.exit('cp-build: receipt drift on contract fields: '+repr({k:(head['data'].get(k),new['data'].get(k)) for k in inv if head['data'].get(k)!=new['data'].get(k)}))\\\"\"\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:534:      \"goal\": \"Author (never run — the dead-last checkpoint runs it) a wedge-safe first-light benchmark of the in-tree USB4 stream primitive, as transport-decision evidence for the morning. Deliverables: (1) bench/usb4stream-bench.py — one file serving both roles (coordinator role is the default; peer role via --role peer --dev PATH; the peer is