{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MCH5eqtRu4XZWAcoa2i2zo","type":"tool_result","content":"bench/run-matrix.sh:440:# data.transport.fn_transport_rung is rail0-sockets — a wire-fallback rung\nbench/run-matrix.sh:559:        \"fn_transport_rung\": os.environ.get(\"TP_RUNG\", \"\"),\nbench/run-matrix.sh:569:             \"when transport.fn_transport_rung is rail0-sockets.\"),\ndocs/DECISIONS-2026-08-30.md:195:records `fn_transport_rung: rail0-sockets`, because a wire-fallback bench is a\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:306:      \"goal\": \"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator files the repo issue). Also write docs/ANNOUNCE.md: a short community post draft describing the setup (two 128 GB unified-memory desktops, two fast rails, one control wire), what was built overnight, where the evidence lives, and where benchmarks land. Boundaries: touch only docs/MORNING.md, docs/ANNOUNCE.md, and docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md.\",\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:391:      \"goal\": \"RE-SCOPED 2026-08-30 (second flow): the package files under host/rdma ALREADY EXIST on main and pass this lane's original acceptance argv verbatim — do NOT rewrite them wholesale, and do not end with an empty diff (the empty-diff completion failure is a known harness hazard). Concrete deliverables now: (1) tests/test_rdma_package.py — the test the original goal promised: assert both pin commits 503c5ae1e72aa9ed91925dafa3d82ee2e992747f and 76ba39b630a70accb72f19388eefe48844b50eb8 appear in host/rdma/fetch-and-build.sh; assert no line of that script begins with insmod or modprobe (optionally sudo-prefixed) — the no-unattended-load invariant, spec F.1; assert host/rdma/attended-bringup.md carries the 'physically present' and 'worker first' language. (2) Fold the odinlink learnings (repo issue 6, evidence at the reference estate the issue names) into host/rdma/ab-protocol.md and host/rdma/attended-bringup.md as short dated appendix sections: terminal-failure framing for verbs init (on ANY init failure: no retry, restore the socket env byte-identical on both ranks, one restart, and the terminal fallback rung is ALWAYS the ethernet wire, never the second rail); the 11 microsecond one-way rail reference figure; the per-cable p2p ceiling asymmetry; and the measured hazard that a verbs transmit toward a closed peer receive ring stalls end-to-end credits and wedges the whole XDomain INCLUDING TCP on the same cable — recovery is reboot-only, which is why no verbs rung may ever appear in an unattended fallback ladder. (3) A dated 'state of tonight' preamble note in attended-bringup.md: no ibverbs device exists on either node right now, the staged module sets cover only kernels 7.1.4 and 7.2.0 while the fleet runs 7.2.2, so the attended morning fetch-and-build on BOTH nodes (running-kernel gate 7.2.2) precedes any A/B; the honest expectation from the one measured community precedent is about +3.4 percent over held TCP — adopt only on a fingerprint-clean counterbalanced majority win. The preamble must ALSO state the Gate 0 transport-rung caveat: the banked socket-transport benchmark that unlocks bring-up must have been measured over the Thunderbolt rail — a bench receipt whose transport record reads fn_transport_rung wire-fallback is a 5GbE artifact and does NOT satisfy Gate 0; on a wire-fallback night the attended morning first heals rail 0 and re-banks a rail-sockets bench before any verbs work. Keep every existing hard rule intact: nothing GPL vendored, nothing installs or loads automatically, one rail only, bring-up starts only after a committed socket-transport benchmark exists under results/. Boundaries: touch only host/rdma and tests/.\",\nREADME.md:169:   into every receipt as `fn_transport_rung` so a wire night can never be\n=== gate0 rdma ===\nab-protocol.md\nattended-bringup.md\nfetch-and-build-nixos.diff\nfetch-and-build.sh\nSCOPING-REPORT.md\n=== bench receipt data fields ===\n# =============================================================================\n# Phase D — the bench.json receipt the receipts gate grades.\n#\n# HONESTY RULE (spec F.8): arms, loads_per_arm, and counterbalanced are\n# DERIVED from the rows actually measured, never stamped from the design.\n# When spec_on died the receipt says so: arms=[\"spec_off\"],\n# counterbalanced=false, spec_on_failed=true, with the failure-log path.\n#\n# TRANSPORT PROVENANCE: this bench.json is the Gate 0 socket-transport\n# artifact host/rdma/attended-bringup.md requires ONLY when\n# data.transport.fn_transport_rung is rail0-sockets — a wire-fallback rung\n# is a 5GbE artifact and does NOT unlock the verbs A/B.\n# =============================================================================\nTP_IFNAME=\"$(podman exec \"$FN_CONTAINER\" printenv NCCL_SOCKET_IFNAME 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nTP_IBDIS=\"$(podman exec \"$FN_CONTAINER\" printenv NCCL_IB_DISABLE 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nTP_RUNG=\"$(podman exec \"$FN_CONTAINER\" printenv FN_TRANSPORT_RUNG 2>/dev/null || true)\"\nexport RECEIPTS BENCH_DIR SERIAL_JSONL SUMMARIES_JSONL DIVERGENT_TXT\nexport LOADS_PER_ARM CONCURRENCY SCHEDULE_DESC SPEC_ON_DEAD\nexport TP_IFNAME TP_IBDIS TP_RUNG\nexport DEPTH_LIST=\"${DEPTHS[*]}\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, json, os, time\n\nbench_dir = os.environ[\"BENCH_DIR\"]\nreceipts = os.environ[\"RECEIPTS\"]\nconcurrency = int(os.environ[\"CONCURRENCY\"])\nschedule = os.environ[\"SCHEDULE_DESC\"].split()\ndepths = [int(x) for x in os.environ[\"DEPTH_LIST\"].split()]\nspec_on_failed = os.environ.get(\"SPEC_ON_DEAD\") == \"1\"\n\ndef read_jsonl(path):\n    if not os.path.exists(path):\n        return []\n    out = []\n    with open(path) as f:\n        for ln in f:\n            ln = ln.strip()\n            if ln:\n                out.append(json.loads(ln))\n    return out","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c18f0a4-02d1-4d56-a81b-3d63fcd0659e","uuid":"6d4965e7-d8f8-4f8f-a0b7-56e8119a8467","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:30:00.078Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"bench/run-matrix.sh:440:# data.transport.fn_transport_rung is rail0-sockets — a wire-fallback rung\nbench/run-matrix.sh:559:        \"fn_transport_rung\": os.environ.get(\"TP_RUNG\", \"\"),\nbench/run-matrix.sh:569:             \"when transport.fn_transport_rung is rail0-sockets.\"),\ndocs/DECISIONS-2026-08-30.md:195:records `fn_transport_rung: rail0-sockets`, because a wire-fallback bench is a\nsilent-factory-worklists/flashnext.json:306:      \"goal\": \"AMENDED 2026-08-30: docs/MORNING.md currently holds the operator's 2026-08-29 day-run stop-state record — FIRST move that file verbatim to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md (git mv, keep every byte), THEN write the new docs/MORNING.md per spec claim 7.1 (specs/flashnext/spec.md#r7). This lane renders BEFORE the milestone checkpoints run (it sits early in the serial graph), so the receipt review table has two row kinds: receipts already banked at render time (build, weights, possibly smoke) carry their observed status and the bound they were graded against; every receipt that lands AFTER render is PRE-DECLARED — one row each for preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, and usb4stream, naming the file path, the bound scripts/receipts-verify.py grades it against, and how to read it. Three pre-declared rows are mandatory and specific: (a) results/receipts/usb4stream.json — cp-usb4stream runs dead-last after cp-close and only when the pair serve is already down; name its three typed outcomes (ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO), say that data.outcome is where to read them, that 'skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable' is the EXPECTED outcome after a healthy night, and that a skipped or aborted outcome is the typed blocker for that step per F.12; (b) results/receipts/failed/ — the quarantine directory: any step that fails its own grading writes its fail receipt THERE so one graded failure cannot redden every later gate run; every file present there in the morning is a typed blocker the operator reviews first; (c) results/receipts/failed/context.json — if present, the honest full-context decode ratio undershot the 0.9 bound (12 full-attention layers walking 256K KV; the community precedent shows about a 2x falloff by 50-73k) — a typed performance finding routed to the optimization menu, deliberately NOT a campaign failure. Also render: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN from the spec with its drain state); the promotion checklist (what the operator verifies before any fleet change, per ruling P13 — and state the causality plainly: the fleet's local-models sync retires any staged artifact that has no catalog row; it pruned the staged checkpoint from BOTH nodes on 08-29 around 20:07/20:14; applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is the act that makes staging durable, and it must precede any rebuild or any restart of the model-sync trigger service); the transport-rung caveat (if any receipt records fn_transport_rung wire-fallback, the night ran on the 5GbE wire: valid but degraded receipts, and bench.json then does NOT satisfy the rail-sockets Gate 0 for verbs bring-up — healing rail 0 is the morning's first transport act); the optimization menu; and a blocker template implementing ruling P16. The optimization menu carries, beyond the original items (tuned mixture-kernel config generation for this GPU, graph-capture matrix, jumbo-frame A-B, draft-length sweep, the four-bit expert lane pointers from IMPORTS.md): the speculative-head depth sweep n in 1 to 4 plus the index-share and padded-drafter knobs (UNKNOWN-5); the attended RDMA go/no-go with the honest cost (2-4 attended hours, two more reboots, worker deploy-path fix first, nothing staged for kernel 7.2.2 yet) and honest expectation (about +3.4 percent measured precedent over held TCP); the stream-primitive morning decision rule (attended port of the reference doorbell allreduce onto the in-tree stream device ONLY if the banked exchange p50 at 8-16 KiB is at or under about 40 microseconds AND the bench matrix shows decode is allreduce-dominated — noting the stream bench likely runs attended in the morning after teardown, since it skips while the pair serves); the full-context decode probe follow-up when deferred; a rejected-with-reason register so nothing is re-litigated (the community int4-WMMA expert lane: bound to a different runtime's artifact, single-device only, unreachable even in its own public release; the indexer rotation plus FP4 QAT art: fidelity art for a different model family's trained indexer graph — our engine's indexer is weight-free bf16 with no such trained graph, so transplanting it would corrupt top-k selection); the load-phase page-cache drop-behind remedy pointer for repo issue 2 (release file pages in chunks behind the loader); a per-shape kernel block-size tuning item for the 2560x640 and 640x2560 expert shapes (community precedent: a forced tile choice beat the auto-selector on exactly these shapes); and a note to audit the drafter hidden-state versus prefix-cache position sync before the speculative profile is declared production (a community v1.1 fix records the failure mode: cached target prefix reused while the drafter state timeline sits elsewhere breaks multi-turn — the operator file