{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYEMz5oQ5CdYC1LVTXus","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Gt375YkbzF9dh6nV7JVK7C","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'\nmorning-ledger: archive the 08-29 halt record, render the ledger and the announce draft\n\ndocs/MORNING.md held the operator's 2026-08-29 halt record. Moved verbatim\n(byte-identical, md5 0635e52d) to docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md, then\nrendered the new ledger per spec claim 7.1.\n\nThis lane runs early in the serial graph, before the milestone checkpoints, so\nthe receipt review carries two row kinds. Banked at render: build.json (pass,\ncontainer lane, 839 s) and the two weight receipts, flagged read-with-suspicion\nuntil cp-weights overwrites the round-1 timestamps the fleet sync invalidated.\nPre-declared: smoke, preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context,\nbench, usb4stream — each with its path, the bound receipts-verify.py grades it\nagainst, and how to read it.\n\nThree pre-declared rows are spelled out in full: usb4stream.json (dead-last\nafter cp-close, idle-cable-only, status always pass, the answer is in\ndata.outcome — ok / skipped:REASON / aborted:PHASE:ERRNO, with\nskipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable the EXPECTED healthy-night outcome and a\nskipped or aborted outcome the typed blocker per F.12); results/receipts/failed/\nas the quarantine directory reviewed first; and failed/context.json as a\ndeferral-typed performance finding routed to the menu, deliberately not a\ncampaign failure.\n\nAlso rendered: the open-items list (every UNKNOWN with its drain state plus the\neight honestly-open items); the P13 promotion checklist, whose step 0 states the\nprune causality plainly — the local-models sync retires any staged artifact with\nno catalog row, it took the checkpoint off both nodes at ~20:07/20:14 on 08-29,\nand applying handoff/catalog-row.patch is what makes staging durable and must\nprecede any rebuild or model-sync restart; the transport-rung caveat (a\nwire-fallback night is valid but degraded and bench.json then does not satisfy\nthe rail-sockets Gate 0); the thirteen-item optimization menu; a\nrejected-with-reason register so the int4-WMMA estate and the indexer\nrotation/FP4 QAT art are never re-litigated; and a P16 blocker template.\n\ndocs/ANNOUNCE.md is the community post draft: the pair, the two rails and the\ncontrol wire, why the fork exists, what the night built, where the evidence\nlives, and where the benchmark numbers land — with the numbers left as explicit\nFILL placeholders and a do-not-post-before-receipts gate at the top.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit status --porcelain; echo \"---\"; git log --oneline -1; git show --stat --oneline HEAD | head","description":"Commit and verify clean tree"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":324,"cache_read_input_tokens":114278,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":324},"output_tokens":17,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c18f0a4-02d1-4d56-a81b-3d63fcd0659e","uuid":"2798623d-ab2e-4b97-aca4-598809339ce3","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:34:50.419Z","request_id":"req_011CeYEMyLA3CxKh8awx9ZWp"}
