{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeYEPAKyXUahqJU6PnCtF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Committed as `bc5c5fe` on `tally-work/flashnext-0c224ca75c49/morning-ledger`; `git status --porcelain` prints nothing.\n\n**What landed** (all three paths inside the write boundary, nothing else touched):\n\n- **`docs/DAYRUN-STOP-STATE-2026-08-29.md`** — the 08-29 halt record moved via `git mv`, byte-identical to `HEAD~1:docs/MORNING.md` (md5 `0635e52d…` verified both sides).\n- **`docs/MORNING.md`** — new ledger. Receipt review in two kinds: banked-at-render (`build.json` pass/839 s; the two weight receipts flagged read-with-suspicion until cp-weights overwrites the round-1 timestamps the fleet sync invalidated) and pre-declared rows for smoke, preflight, proxy, tp2, residency, fidelity, context, bench, usb4stream — each naming its path, the exact bound `scripts/receipts-verify.py` enforces, and how to read it. The three mandated rows are spelled out: `usb4stream.json` (dead-last, idle-cable-only, `status` always pass, answer in `data.outcome` with the three typed shapes, `skipped:serve-up-on-shared-cable` pre-declared as the expected healthy-night outcome and a skip/abort as the F.12 typed blocker); `results/receipts/failed/` as the quarantine directory read first; `failed/context.json` as a deferral-typed performance finding routed to the menu. Plus open items (every UNKNOWN with drain state, and the eight still-open), the P13 promotion checklist with the prune causality and `handoff/catalog-row.patch` as step 0 before any rebuild or sync restart, the transport-rung caveat and its Gate 0 consequence, a 13-item optimization menu, the rejected-with-reason register, and a P16 blocker template.\n- **`docs/ANNOUNCE.md`** — community post draft with the numbers as explicit `[FILL: …]` placeholders and a do-not-post-before-receipts gate.\n\n**Checks:** both acceptance argv exit 0; `scripts/receipts-verify.py` clean (3 receipts, 0 violations); `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` — 54 tests OK.\n\nOne judgment call worth flagging: the ledger references `handoff/catalog-row.patch`, `docs/USB4STREAM-TRANSPORT.md`, and the `usb4stream` receipts bound as things that do not exist yet — they are owned by the `catalog-handoff` and `usb4stream-bench` lanes, which run in the same graph. Writing them as forward references was the only option inside this task's boundary, and the ledger says explicitly which rows are forecasts rather than observations."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1284,"cache_read_input_tokens":114602,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1284},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1c18f0a4-02d1-4d56-a81b-3d63fcd0659e","uuid":"8f582dda-6ca9-46ff-9f91-9bf1efe0c4d4","timestamp":"2026-08-30T03:35:06.092Z","request_id":"req_011CeYEP9MCDP9sqF64GEdTD"}
